.DS_Store

# Jekyll build output
_site/
.jekyll-cache/
.jekyll-metadata

# Agent / editor local state — per-machine, never shared
.claude/
CLAUDE.md

# CLAUDE.md is tracked deliberately: it carries the project-authored
# Planner/Coder convention below Bram's marker block. The bram:start block
# itself is only a 3-line import, so it does not churn the way AGENTS.md did.
!CLAUDE.md
resources/
.bram.json
.obsidian/

# Bram Setup rewrites AGENTS.md's <!-- bram:start --> block on every upgrade.
# Ignored rather than tracked, which REVERSES the decision in PR #12 ("track the
# Bram Setup block"). #12's goal was a clean `git status`, and committing the
# block only achieves that between upgrades — each upgrade produces a diff
# somebody has to notice and commit, forever. Ignoring the file achieves the
# same goal permanently and with no recurring chore.
#
# Nothing is lost by not tracking it: the block describes Bram's codex
# developer_instructions path while this repo runs Claude Code, and the real
# enforcement lives in .claude/settings.json with the working conventions in
# .claude/bram-conventions.md — both per-machine and already untracked. The
# committed block was therefore neither accurate nor load-bearing.
AGENTS.md
